From 743d95b4f9c811d701d2f3590182a827661da84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:12:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Isolate notification subscription revisions and
 private reader memos

Problem: unrelated board content commits repeatedly scanned every notification
subscription; private cached_ro fallbacks displaced the retained shared memo.

Why: covered_revision(table) checks coverage but returns the global annotation
counter. Titles, comments and runs move it. A private fallback was unconditionally
published then closed, so the next shared read reset event history to zero.
Root (happened): invalidation scope and reader custody did not match memo inputs.
Root (not caught): existing no-rescan tests/benchmark only exercised claim_expires
bookkeeping and subscription cursor changes, not unrelated substantive writes or
shared/private signature publication. Earlier 622dc84/e8d9f6b/438f8a4 retained this
coupling. Historical cause of all serve timeouts remains undetermined.

Add an independent notify counter with exact SQL coverage for six read columns,
installed/repaired transactionally by writable board init. Unknown coverage keeps
literal fresh reads. Read coverage/counter/rows in one snapshot. Missing-counter
repair changes schema generation too. Generic revision triggers stay unchanged.
Only retained shared readers publish signature memos; private results stay local.
No timeout, polling interval, delivery or at-most-once semantics change.

Proof:
- Authentic predecessor RED: title/comment/run rescan and private publication
  assertions failed; heartbeat negative control passed.
- Canonical focused consumers: 185 passed across 13 files (pre-expansion).
- Expanded notify pair: 36 passed, including actual SQL counts, every read column,
  legacy/partial/foreign schema, repair rollback, missing-row reuse, WAL/DB and
  same-file connection replacement, concurrent commit and private contention.
- 16 exact-anchor mutants killed; two original survivors received explicit
  no-write foreign-schema and snapshot-boundary assertions and were re-killed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks passed.
- Synthetic 2,887 TUI / 8,748 total subscriptions, 10k events, 200 unrelated title
  commits x 10 chat polls: read thread CPU 720.338 -> 83.413 ms; full-subscription
  scans 200 -> 0, inflight scans 200 -> 0, same signatures/event highwater.
  Writer CPU excluded; this is not whole-serve or incident recovery proof.

Incident owner retains final-process authenticated endpoint measurements and
unchanged 30-minute detector acceptance after natural deployment.
